---
import GlossaryEntry from '../../layouts/GlossaryEntry.astro';
---
<GlossaryEntry
  category="ESP32"
  title="Partition Scheme"
  subtitle="How the ESP32's flash memory is divided between the sketch, filesystem, and OTA"
  backTo="/guides/max98357a-littlefs#uploading"
  backLabel="Back"
  highlights={[
    'The ESP32 has 4MB of flash - the partition scheme decides how it is split',
    'No OTA / 2MB SPIFFS gives the best balance for LittleFS audio',
    'Change it in Arduino IDE under Tools → Partition Scheme',
    'Changing the scheme requires a full reflash of the sketch',
  ]}
>
  <Fragment slot="desc">
    <p>The ESP32 has 4MB of flash memory. A partition scheme is a layout that divides that space between different uses - the compiled sketch (app), the filesystem (LittleFS/SPIFFS), OTA update storage, and a small area for settings (NVS). The scheme you choose directly affects how much space is available for audio files.</p>

    <h2>How to change it</h2>
    <p>In Arduino IDE, go to <strong>Tools &rarr; Partition Scheme</strong> and select the scheme before compiling and uploading. After changing the scheme you must reflash the sketch - the IDE will prompt you if needed.</p>

    <h2>Which scheme to use for LittleFS audio</h2>
    <p>For the MAX98357A LittleFS audio guide, the recommended scheme is <strong>No OTA (2MB APP / 2MB SPIFFS)</strong>. The I2S audio sketch is small so 2MB of app space is more than enough, and 2MB of LittleFS gives the most room for audio files.</p>

    <div class="scheme-table">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Scheme</th><th>App space</th><th>LittleFS space</th><th>OTA</th><th>Audio at 44100Hz</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>No OTA (2MB APP / 2MB SPIFFS)</strong></td><td>2MB</td><td>2MB</td><td>No</td><td>~22 seconds</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Default (4MB with SPIFFS)</td><td>1.2MB</td><td>1.5MB</td><td>No</td><td>~17 seconds</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Huge APP (3MB No OTA / 1MB SPIFFS)</td><td>3MB</td><td>1MB</td><td>No</td><td>~11 seconds</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Minimal SPIFFS (1.9MB APP with OTA)</td><td>1.9MB</td><td>~600KB</td><td>Yes</td><td>~7 seconds</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="callout callout-tip">
      <strong>Drop to 22050Hz for speech.</strong>
      Audio sizes above are for 44100Hz 16-bit mono. Drop to 22050Hz and every number roughly doubles - the No OTA scheme gives you around 45 seconds of clear speech audio. Change <code>-ar</code> in your ffmpeg command and <code>SAMPLE_RATE</code> in the sketch to match.
    </div>

    <h2>What OTA means</h2>
    <p>OTA (Over The Air) update support requires a second copy of the app partition so the ESP32 can receive a new sketch over WiFi while still running the old one. That overhead costs about 1MB of flash. For LittleFS audio there is no benefit - skip OTA and get more audio space.</p>

    <h2>What NVS is</h2>
    <p>NVS (Non-Volatile Storage) is a small reserved area where the ESP32 stores settings that survive a reboot - WiFi credentials, calibration values, that sort of thing. It is always present regardless of scheme and is too small to be useful for audio.</p>
  </Fragment>
</GlossaryEntry>

